-- title:
--   Level drop from Γ₀(N) to Γ₀(N/p) in characteristic p
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $p$ be a prime with $K$ of characteristic $p$, and let $N$ be a nonzero natural number such that $p^2 \mid N$. For a subgroup $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) is the intermediate field of $K((q)) =$ `LaurentSeries K` generated over $K$ by the set [`ModularCurve.intFormRatiosC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L83), namely by those Laurent series of the form $\overline{p_f}/\overline{p_g}$ where $k$ is an integer, $f$ and $g$ are modular forms of weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, $p_f$ and $p_g$ are power series with integer coefficients satisfying the predicate [`ModularCurve.IsIntegralQExp`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L37) with respect to $f$ and $g$ (that is, the $q$-expansion of the form at $\infty$, taken with period $1$, is the image of the integral power series), $\overline{\phantom{x}}$ denotes [`ModularCurve.intSeriesC K`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L69), the coefficientwise reduction of an integral power series into a Laurent series over $K$, and $\overline{p_g} \neq 0$. The assertion is the equality of intermediate fields $$\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,K\,\Gamma_0(N) = \mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,K\,\Gamma_0(N/p),$$ with $\Gamma_0$ the congruence subgroups `CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0` and $N/p$ natural division.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$p$ level-lowering phenomenon for $q$-expansion function fields: when $p^2 \mid N$, reducing $q$-expansions modulo $p$ cannot distinguish level $\Gamma_0(N)$ from level $\Gamma_0(N/p)$, the mechanism being that $U_p$ inverts the Frobenius twist on reduced $q$-expansions. It is used in the proofs that the modular function field in characteristic $2$ and in characteristic $3$ is separably generated by the relevant coordinate at level $H$.
